EXPECTED RED: `refile = 404, want 200`. The `len(visits) < 2` guard is deliberate: it is the same shape as R6's `before == 0`, and it is what stops the leg passing vacuously if the fixture changes.

OTHER LEGS: a refile that CREATES an occasion — the client supplies visitId and visitAt, and the ordinals of that place's visits come back rewritten in `at` DESC with the new one in its right position; a refile out of a place leaves the OLD place's visit standing, because the visit belongs to the trip and not to the photograph; a caption of whitespace stores NULL; snooze with three known ids and two unknown ones snoozes three, skips two, bumps the version ONCE, and answers 200; snooze matching nothing writes nothing and does not bump; a dismissed walk still comes back from the read with its points intact; deleting a photograph answers 204 with a new ETag and leaves no dangling reference.

